Article 6 (Meetings)
(1) The chairperson shall convene a meeting of the Committee in any of the following cases: <Amended on May 1, 2020>
1. Where the Minister of the National Court Administration requests deliberation or advice concerning the architectural planning of a courthouse building or other relevant matters;
2. Where the chairperson deems a meeting necessary.
(2) Meetings of the Committee shall open with the attendance of a majority of its incumbent members, and resolutions shall be adopted with the affirmative vote of a majority of members present. Where the votes are equally divided, the chairperson shall have the deciding vote.
(3) Where necessary, the Committee may have the presiding senior judge or the director of the administrative bureau of the court concerned with the courthouse construction, or interested parties such as local governments involved in a courthouse relocation, attend a meeting to present their opinions.
(4) Committee meetings shall not be open to the public: Provided, That minutes of meetings containing the following matters shall be prepared and preserved, and meetings may be audio-recorded or video-recorded where deemed necessary. <Newly inserted on May 1, 2020>
1. Date, time, and place of the meeting;
2. List of members participating in deliberation;
3. Agenda items for deliberation and details thereof;
4. Results of resolutions.
